{
  "title": "Regular Expression Matching",
  "description": "Decide whether a pattern `p` matches a string `s`. The pattern is made of lowercase letters and two special characters:\n\n- `.` matches any single character.\n- `*` means \"zero or more copies of the character just before it\". For example, `a*` matches an empty string, `a`, `aa`, and so on, and `.*` matches any string at all.\n\nThe pattern must match the **whole** string, not just part of it. Return `true` if it does and `false` otherwise.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `0 <= s.size() <= 20`, and `s` contains only lowercase English letters.\n- `0 <= p.size() <= 20`, and `p` contains only lowercase English letters, `.`, and `*`.\n- Every `*` in `p` comes directly after a letter or a `.`.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "bool regex_match(string s, string p) {\n    int n = s.size(), m = p.size();\n    vector<vector<bool>> ok(n + 1, vector<bool>(m + 1, false));\n    ok[n][m] = true;\n    for (int i = n; i >= 0; --i) {\n        for (int j = m - 1; j >= 0; --j) {\n            bool first = i < n && (p[j] == s[i] || p[j] == '.');\n            if (j + 1 < m && p[j + 1] == '*') {\n                ok[i][j] = ok[i][j + 2] || (first && ok[i + 1][j]);\n            } else {\n                ok[i][j] = first && ok[i + 1][j + 1];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return ok[0][0];\n}\n",
  "template": "bool regex_match(string s, string p) {\n    // Return whether the pattern p matches all of s.\n    return false;\n}\n",
  "tags": [
    "Strings",
    "Recursion",
    "Dynamic Programming"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "test_number": 0,
      "explanation": "c* can stand for zero copies of c, a* for two copies of a, and b matches the final b. Together they match the whole string aab."
    },
    {
      "test_number": 1,
      "explanation": "The pattern is a single a, which matches only one character. The string has two, so the whole string is not matched."
    }
  ],
